{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794008018,"nonce":"YTF44CSnNGy7akrR2uzmCNFPwtM=","message":"Flat float array part landed on top of the integer one (instructions retired, Mac cranelift-only zylua, vs the commit before the flat arrays).\n\nFill and sum of 3M floats: 1.9G to 0.48G instructions, peak RSS 271 MB to 89 MB. a[i] = a[i] + 1.0 over 14k elements: -41%. pipeline: 2.75G to 2.07G (-26%). Matrix multiply, nbody, mandelbrot, binary_trees, collatz, fib, records, tokenize level.\n\nA typed read of a flat element widens to the read's static type without a box; only an Any read allocates. A first version boxed every non-exact read type and cost 2.5x on a float sum.\n\nMixed int and float stores into a flat array convert it to boxes (one way). Open: flat paths in table.sort/insert/remove/concat/unpack (they convert today), no-scan allocation of the flat buffer, and the allocations per small constructor table (header, arr box, list header, buffer).","files":null}]}